    descriptionEn: "Drone rock emerged in mid-1960s England and America, deriving its name from the aeronautical term describing aircraft engine's continuous humming sound. This revolutionary genre arose from the convergence of Indian classical music (particularly the tampura's sustained tones), German krautrock, and experimental minimalism. Production emphasized spatial depth and sonic texture over traditional song structures. Culturally, it reflected 1960s countercultural movements, Eastern philosophical influence, and rejection of conventional pop music, inspiring later shoegaze, post-rock, and doom metal genres while establishing precedent for ambient and experimental music.",
