    descriptionEn: "Indie folk crystallized in the early 2000s across the United States and United Kingdom, merging traditional folk's authenticity with alternative rock's independent ethos. The term marries «independent» (from major labels) and «folk» (music of the people), embodying a DIY approach to narrative songcraft. Born from the intersection of 1960s folk revival and 1990s indie rock scenes, this genre draws from Bob Dylan's legacy while embracing contemporary sonic innovations. Culturally, indie folk represents an authenticity quest in our digital age, favoring intimate venues over stadiums. It channels environmental and social consciousness, becoming the voice of a generation seeking communal values against contemporary individualism, while celebrating craftsmanship and storytelling traditions in an increasingly automated musical landscape.",
